    "message": "fix(rotation): correct credential health defects and attribute requests to keys\n\nAudited the credential rotation engine and fixed five defects, each verified\nwith a repro before and a regression test after.\n\n- acquire() returned early for the ``single`` policy and for one-key pools,\n  skipping all usage bookkeeping. Since ``single`` is the default policy, every\n  default install reported zero requests per credential.\n- A client disconnect mid-stream reported neither success nor failure, so a\n  half-open credential kept its ``is_probing`` reservation forever and was\n  never selectable again. Added a synchronous ``release_probe`` (awaiting is\n  unsafe while GeneratorExit propagates) called from the stream's finally.\n- Failures after the first chunk were never reported, so a credential that\n  consistently died mid-stream accrued no failures and never cooled down.\n- Auth lockout tiers were indexed by ``consecutive_failures``, which non-auth\n  errors also increment: two 5xx plus one 401 jumped straight to the 24-hour\n  tier. Auth escalation now tracks its own counter.\n- The rotating wrapper's already-attempted fallback reached past the pool for\n  an untried index, bypassing the health checks; it now stops instead.\n\nPer-key analytics, mirroring what websearch analytics already does:\n\n- ``requests`` gains nullable ``key_index``/``key_label`` columns, added by an\n  explicit ALTER TABLE since CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS is a no-op on existing\n  databases. The stats covering index is versioned so it is rebuilt with\n  ``key_label`` rather than silently kept without it.\n- ``stats()`` returns a ``by_key`` breakdown and both endpoints accept a\n  ``key`` filter; the Requests tab gains a Key column, filter, and panel.\n- The credential chosen deep in the provider stack reaches the request log via\n  a mutable per-request slot, so no provider signature changes. Only the index\n  and a masked ``first4…last4`` label are stored; the raw key never is.\n\n``mask_key_label`` moves to its neutral owner beside ``parse_credential_keys``.\nAlso documents provider multi-key rotation in .env.example, which covered only\nthe websearch equivalents.",
